            <ArticleTitle>Chest pain in the emergency department.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>178-83</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The assessment of patients with chest pain is challenging for any emergency physician because of the spectrum of illness covered by this symptom. Patients may have a serious life-threatening condition or a trivial self-limiting illness. This article presents an approach to the assessment and early management of patients presenting with acute non-traumatic chest pain in the emergency department.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
